{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"STATUS: NOT STARTED. Unsigned, deliberately queued behind 2b16-9be0-a8f5-41d9.\n\nReparented under epic e369-a449-4773-48fb by operator ruling (all three J11-surfaced defects gate that\nepic). File impact is already declared, so the plan review can be run immediately — but see below.\n\n**DO NOT START THIS BEFORE 2b16 LANDS.** Both tickets modify `inbound_differ.py`; running them in\nparallel would collide. 2b16 is claimed and ready to implement; land it first.\n\nTHE DEFECT, traced: an inbound parent CLEAR is dropped by TWO independent layers —\n`fetcher.py:508-511` omits an absent parent from the snapshot, so the clear is invisible downstream,\nand `inbound_differ.py:266-270` then refuses `parent_id=None` so nothing is emitted. The APPLY layer\nis already capable of handling it, which is what makes this purely a detection gap.\n\nA LIVE ORACLE ALREADY EXISTS AND IS EXPECTED RED:\n`tests/external/live_jira_dc/test_dc_mutations.py::test_inbound_clear_parent_round_trips`, asserting\n`fields.parent` / `.parent_id` is falsy after the parent was proven present. Do NOT edit or invert it.\n\nONE PLATFORM UNKNOWN the harness must settle, recorded by the agent that wrote the cell: whether DC\naccepts nulling a sub-task's `fields.parent` at all. The cell reports that case as an explicit\n`SETUP FAILED` message, so the first red will name which of the two situations it is rather than\nlooking like a bridge defect. Read that before concluding the fix is wrong."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785725152675839001,"uuid":"f08d8531-b1bb-4d72-ad76-58a386edd775"}